## TODO: pak-conflict-detection

Phase 4, the only modrex-main change of the pak manifest feature. Blocked until the
three TODOs above (pak-analyzer, pak-entries-schema, manifest-backfill-and-size) are
done and index.db actually carries pak_entries. Applies to PD3 and Crime Boss only;
both are UE 4.27.2, so one format generation.

### src-tauri/src/commands/mod_index.rs
- Query: entries (paths) for a given content sha256
- Query: given the set of installed mods' hashes, find asset paths claimed by more than one

### Install-time conflict warning
- All install entry points (BrowsePage, ModDetailPage header, DownloadsTab): before
  install, look up the new mod's entry paths and warn "overrides X, also overridden by
  installed mod Y". Warn only, never block the install.

### InstalledPage
- Health indicator for installed mods with overlapping asset paths

### Honesty rule
- A pak whose manifest status is encrypted / no-directory-index must surface as
  "contents unknown", never as "no conflicts"

### Follow-up (separate, later)
- Fuzzy identification: match repackaged/renamed paks by entry-set fingerprint when the
  outer sha256 misses

